<title>GERMANY: Phoenix buys Hungarian rubber processor.</title>
<headline>Phoenix buys Hungarian rubber processor.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German rubber company Phoenix AG said on Thursday it has bought Hungarian rubber processor Taurus Holding and its subsidiaries Taurus Palma and Taurus Emerge.</p>
<p>The companies were bought through Hungarian privatisation programmes, Phoenix said in a statement.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Phoenix said it expected the two Taurus units to report sales growth of about 20 percent for 1996 and for growth rates to remain high in the coming zears.</p>
<p>Phoenix reported a 1995 profit of 5.7 million marks on sales of 1.44 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
